# A Room has two names and a player naming it names one of them (CR 709.4a); an object has the chosen name if one of its names is
# it. Bot1's Anointed Peacekeeper names Unholy Annex, so on turn 2 Bot2 may not cast the Annex door: with only a Swamp and Black Lotus
# (four mana) the spell would cost {2}{B} + {2} = 5 (the refusal). Naming the other door instead (the next scenario) leaves it at 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Anointed Peacekeeper
Plains x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Black Lotus
Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber
Swamp x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Anointed Peacekeeper.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Name(Unholy Annex)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
! Bot2.Hand.Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber.Cast(Ability: Unholy Annex)

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 2
